  "denominator_policy": "Supported-view accuracy is labelled by answer vocabulary (7,714 top-100 or 9,823 top-1000); only raw-distribution accuracy on the common 10,004-row development view is a Pareto axis.",
  "measurement_class_policy": "Headline latency uses only E7b/E9 END_TO_END_SERIAL warm medians. otter155 and otter159 are separate blocks; the -18.69% fusion bridge failed the ±10% gate, so no node merge or adjustment factor is allowed. Cold, memory, QPS, checkpoint-byte, cached/head-only and E7a additive headline values are absent.",
  "pairing_policy": "Seven E9 re-timed reference rows are PAIRING_UNRESOLVED and receive no E9 accuracy value. E7b product accuracy 0.49050 and E9 product latency 6.1990 ms are separate facts, never a paired E9 coordinate. Only the four SmolVLM rows carry paired E9 raw accuracy.",
  "parameter_policy": "Trainable parameter count and total loaded parameter count are distinct retained fields. Total loaded parameters are not model size, storage, checkpoint bytes, VRAM or measured memory; nominal family labels are separate. No new parameter ratio is derived.",
  "ratio_policy": "The only ratio reported is the stored canonical wording that SmolVLM-500M constrained was approximately 24.7 times slower in same-node warm serial latency. No ratio is recomputed.",
  "environmental_cost_policy": "Energy, power, carbon and monetary cost were not measured; negative boundary wording is allowed and no affirmative claim is made.",
